alright time for audience questions  we've got three good ones first one I  don't know what's going to happen I  predict many many dislikes no matter  what my answer is to this question Chris  wrote in and other people have as well  and Chris said David where are you on  the Sam cedar versus Jimmy Dore debate  which side are you on for people who  don't know Sam cedar is the host of the  majority report podcast and for he's  formerly of Air America and MSNBC  contributor multiple voices he does on  Bob's Burgers etcetera friend of mine  Jimmy Dore is the host of I think it's  the Jimmy Dore shut every door show  Jimmy door show which is under the young  turks umbrella i believe and they've  been kind of going at it and they've  been going at it for even since before  the election and i think before the  election they debated a Bernie or bust  or not and I think if I recall correctly  Jimmy Dore was a Bernie ER Buster and  Sam cedar was not who said no that  doesn't really make any sense that's  that that's not a good idea and they  debated there and then recently they  also had another one of these flare-ups  I guess you would call them and anyway  that the the left left-wing media  particularly online left-wing media has  sort of split up into these different  factions and I think it's totally  destructive and I'm also going to  participate in that now by taking aside  so blame me for what I'm criticizing no  doubt no listen I'm if I had to pick a  side I'm on the Sam cedar side I don't  think that would be a surprise to  anybody on this i I've been following  both I watch about equal amounts of both  jimmy dore and sam cedar and i think  that sam is doing a completely different  type of thing than Jimmy is I don't I  just flat-out don't agree with Jimmy  with a lot of his I guess they would be  called analyses when it comes to Trump  Russia I think that he's been going out  of his way sort of to almost Mock the  idea that there is anything there with  the Russia story when listen we've got  multiple indictments Michael Flynn is on  the chopping block all this crazy stuff  is going on you know and I also do think  that Sam is not doing politics in a way  that is destructive to the movement of  the  I question whether Jimmy's brand of  politics and the way he does it is  actually counterproductive to the left  because I think he and I would probably  agree that the Democratic Party does  need to move to the left like he and I  wouldn't disagree on that but I think  that the approach he takes is one that  is actually going to further the divide  actually rather than actually try to fix  the problem that the left is dealing  with right now so when you talk about  the split when it comes to progressive  talk shows do you mean the Hillary and  Bernie wings do you mean the sjw types  versus the more free speech absolutist  do you mean those who believe in and  agree with the Russia story versus those  who deny it  I don't think it's one thing and I think  it's bigger than the Democratic Party  because there are elements of the left  that are outside the Democratic Party  right so yes they're within the  Democratic Party there's debate as to  whether it's Democrats Inc or do we need  a more progressive Democratic Party etc  etc abundantly clear that public opinion  on issues tells us that the Democratic  Party does need to move to the left but  there are also people on the Left that  are outside the Democratic Party who  would never consider even voting for a  Democrat because they see the party in  and of itself as part of the problem  that's not an illegitimate position to  take you can take that position and  defend it and I think that's interesting  I've never been a Democrat right I  completely respect that point of view  but I don't think it's just it's very  easy to characterize it as the  authoritarian left versus the non  authoritarian left or the sjw's versus  the non sjws or the regressive left  versus the non regressive 